@host = http://localhost:5211

# Walk-through of the whole online flow against the running API + PostgreSQL.
# Run the requests in order (VS Code "REST Client" extension, or Visual
# Studio's HTTP editor). IDs below assume a freshly created database: the
# first player/guild/adventurer/quest get id 1, the next ones 2, 3...

### 1. Register a player (creates a row in the "players" table)
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "melvin", "email": "melvin@example.com", "password": "secret123" }

### 2. Log in (same credentials)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "melvin", "password": "secret123" }

### 3. Create a guild (starts with 500 gold, 20 food, 10 potions)
POST {{host}}/guilds
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerId": 1, "name": "Guilde de Tartaros" }

### 4. Recruit adventurers (ids 1, 2, 3)
POST {{host}}/guilds/1/adventurers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerId": 1, "name": "Bram", "category": "Warrior" }

###
POST {{host}}/guilds/1/adventurers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerId": 1, "name": "Elara", "category": "Healer" }

###
POST {{host}}/guilds/1/adventurers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerId": 1, "name": "Sameth", "category": "Special", "specialKey": "Sameth" }

### 5. A special adventurer can't be recruited twice in the same guild (expects 409 Conflict)
POST {{host}}/guilds/1/adventurers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerId": 1, "name": "Sameth bis", "category": "Special", "specialKey": "Sameth" }

### 6. List the guild's adventurers
GET {{host}}/guilds/1/adventurers

### 7. Let the API generate today's quests (generation is done server-side)
POST {{host}}/guilds/1/quests/generate

### 8. List today's quests
GET {{host}}/guilds/1/quests?day=1&playerId=1

### 9. Send a team on quest 1 (Escort, needs a Warrior)
POST {{host}}/quests/1/attempt
Content-Type: application/json

{ "adventurerIds": [1, 2] }

### 10. Check the shared guild state (gold/food/hours updated in the database)
GET {{host}}/guilds/1

### 11. Advance to the next day
POST {{host}}/guilds/1/advance-day

### 12. Evaluate the ending (only meaningful from day 10 on)
POST {{host}}/guilds/1/evaluate-ending
